    "created_at": "2021-12-01T22:54:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-12-01T22:57:31Z",
    "body": "Maybe git2 is just very broken? I have this issue with submodules (which aren't really worktrees but they both use `gitdir:` .git files that serve as symlinks iirc) and `Repository::discovery(dir).workdir()` as returned by `context.get_repo()` (that all the git modules except git_status use) results in a completely nonsensical value.\r\n\r\nFor example, with my repo in `~/repo/submodules/subrepo` and a gitdir that points to `~/repo/.git/modules/submodules/subrepo`, `workdir()` returns `Some(\"~/repo/.git/modules/submodules/\")` instead???\r\n\r\nInterestingly, I do have a worktree that appears to work properly. its `gitdir` is an absolute path though, while the submodule I mentioned above uses relative paths. Not sure if that's relevant...",
