    "updated_at": "2021-12-02T16:29:09Z",
    "body": "> Hmmm... I checked the worktree's .git file, and it contains an absolute path.\r\n\r\nIt might be worth checking `.git/worktrees/$treename/gitdir`, `commondir`, and `.git/config` - I've seen issues before where [`config.worktree`](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-config#Documentation/git-config.txt-coreworktree) ended up being set to odd relative paths or something.\r\n\r\nHowever, I think the most consistent way to address this might be what I hinted to in my PR:\r\n\r\n> a more consistent approach might be to just store the git2::Repository inside the Repo directly\r\n\r\nThis would at least completely remove inconsistencies where git2 is unable to open the repo a second time altogether. Storing the original path used to open the repo might also help.",
